<title>UK: Britannic Assurance chief to retire.</title>
<headline>Britannic Assurance chief to retire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britannic Assurance's chief executive Anthony Jefferson has chosen to retire from the company's board at the end of this year, it said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The company said Jefferson would be succeeded by Brian Shaw.</p>
<p>Shaw would retain his present role as appointed actuary of the the firm until new lines of organisational authority were established, Britannic said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44-171-542 7717</p>
